WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.279
- [Interviewer] Cynthia.

00:00:02.279 --> 00:00:03.112
- Yes.

00:00:03.112 --> 00:00:03.945
- [Interviewer] Cynthia,
where you from originally?

00:00:03.945 --> 00:00:04.778
- Santa Barbara.

00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:05.611
- [Interviewer] Santa Barbara.

00:00:05.611 --> 00:00:06.444
And how long have you been
down here in Skid Row?

00:00:06.444 --> 00:00:07.277
- [Cynthia] Seven years.

00:00:07.277 --> 00:00:09.290
- [Interviewer] Seven years.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.690
And what is your drug of choice?

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.523
- [Cynthia] Heroin.

00:00:11.523 --> 00:00:12.681
- [Interviewer] Heroin?

00:00:12.681 --> 00:00:15.383
What age did you first get into drugs?

00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:19.810
- Oh, I started probably
when I was 13 with weed

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.190
and then and then coke, PCP
and then it just escalated

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.571
when I turned 20, I tried
heroin once, I didn't like it,

00:00:27.571 --> 00:00:28.830
believe it or not.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.060
And I left Santa Barbara,
I moved back to L.A.,

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.730
to go stay with my mom for three years

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.780
and then went back to Santa Barbara

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.770
and all my friends were using.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.293
So I just, it's been my whole
life and it's just terrible.

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:42.560
It's a blink of an eye.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.022
- [Interviewer] You ever overdose?

00:00:44.022 --> 00:00:45.160
- Oh God, yeah.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.362
Many times.

00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:47.750
- [Interviewer] What's that like?

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.583
- I think you don't know

00:00:48.583 --> 00:00:49.416
cause you don't remember none of it.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.692
There's several times
I've got up off the ground

00:00:50.692 --> 00:00:52.678
and looking for my shit and they're like

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:53.580
"bitch, don't you know you just OD'd?"

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.121
You don't really remember it.

00:00:56.121 --> 00:00:56.954
- [Interviewer] You're just out.

00:00:56.954 --> 00:00:58.113
- You're just gone, yeah.

00:01:00.781 --> 00:01:02.200
- [Interviewer] And have
you ever been clean?

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.033
- Yeah.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.710
Yeah, I managed a sober
living home in Santa Barbara

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.370
called Woodridge, I worked at the airport,

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:11.370
I had two full-time jobs and I relapsed.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.560
I got off parole and I
wanted to move up north

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.850
to be with a friend of mine
and I gave two weeks notice

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.370
and moved up there and relapsed up north.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.970
And this was part of that still.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.150
I went from there to
San Diego to a program

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.280
to try to quit and that didn't work

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.203
and I was on my way back to Santa Barbara,

00:01:26.203 --> 00:01:28.410
I had a 40 minute layover here in L.A.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.370
and I never got back on the bus.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:32.123
That's how I got stuck down here.

00:01:32.123 --> 00:01:32.956
- [Interviewer] And where
are you staying now?

00:01:32.956 --> 00:01:33.789
On the street?

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:34.622
- On the street.

00:01:34.622 --> 00:01:35.455
- [Interviewer] Do you have a tent or?

00:01:35.455 --> 00:01:36.630
- I have a tent.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:37.646
They're trying to get me housing.

00:01:37.646 --> 00:01:39.397
Sometimes I'm hard to reach

00:01:39.397 --> 00:01:41.200
because they steal my
phones left and right,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.530
you can't keep nothing.

00:01:44.461 --> 00:01:46.280
So we're back on that again,

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.850
so I just got in contact with everybody

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.190
and they're like "damn Cynthia,

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:52.397
you missed like six
referrals to go somewhere".

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.280
So hopefully Tuesday I have an appointment

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.052
we'll see what happens.

00:01:58.052 --> 00:01:58.995
- [Interviewer] Good luck.

00:01:58.995 --> 00:02:00.414
- Yeah.

00:02:00.414 --> 00:02:04.185
- [Interviewer] And then
tell me about your childhood,

00:02:04.185 --> 00:02:05.290
you had one parent, both parents?

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.140
- I had both parents until I was 10

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.683
and my dad was an alcoholic.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.020
They got divorced.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:12.920
She remarried.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.670
That's how I ended up in L.A.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.138
and my dad continued on and he went

00:02:17.138 --> 00:02:18.720
and he finally got clean and sober.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.300
He went to AA and so he was
19 years clean and sober

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.133
when he died.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.890
So I know AA like the back of my hand,

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.070
I know when I'm pulling
the wool over my eyes.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.800
You know, I can't fool myself

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.550
but I still go through the motions.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:35.827
Yeah.

00:02:35.827 --> 00:02:37.420
- [Interviewer] Do you
have children of your own?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.990
- I have three, I didn't raise them.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.140
I wasn't capable of doing that.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.970
Drugs just had me.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.090
- [Interviewer] So are
they in foster care?

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.562
- [Cynthia] My aunt raised
my two youngest girls

00:02:48.562 --> 00:02:53.562
and my old man, my boyfriend's
mother raised my son.

00:02:53.976 --> 00:02:57.130
- [Interviewer] Do you
ever talk to your kids?

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:57.963
- [Cynthia] No, hardly ever.

00:02:57.963 --> 00:03:00.200
I think my son's in prison.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.630
My daughters are, they're just saying

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.160
how they're sick of it.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.610
Cause I'm on and off on and off.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.240
There was a time I was
clean for like three years.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.680
My grandfather was dying of cancer

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.790
and he asked me if I could
help him, take care of him,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.900
and so I cleaned up, got on
methadone and took care of him.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.560
And during that period
of time I saw my girls

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:22.560
and on a regular basis and I
was molested by my grandfather.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.355
And so I always talked
to my kids about that.

00:03:25.355 --> 00:03:27.304
- [Interviewer] What age were you?

00:03:27.304 --> 00:03:28.945
- I don't even know when it started.

00:03:28.945 --> 00:03:31.182
But I think it started awful young.

00:03:31.182 --> 00:03:32.770
Anyway, I was about nine

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.020
and so I used to always
talk to my girls about that.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.670
And I went to visit them one time

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.080
and my oldest daughter told me

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.040
that her uncle was touching them.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.240
And so I didn't know what to do.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.100
I called the police.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.350
I had investigation, whatever
and so now I'm the bad guy

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.310
and my uncle got eight
months work furlough.

00:03:54.287 --> 00:03:56.253
So he really didn't do no jail time.

00:03:57.897 --> 00:03:59.750
None of my kids, nobody
talks to me anymore

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.250
cause I called the cops.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:02.230
I didn't know what else to do.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.833
- [Interviewer] Yeah, well
you did the right thing.

00:04:04.952 --> 00:04:07.052
What would you say to your kids right now?

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.832
- I would just want them to know

00:04:10.832 --> 00:04:15.700
that I didn't purposely
choose drugs over them.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:16.840
You know, I can't explain it

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:21.000
but it's just an overwhelming
obsession to use.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.020
And once I got started, I couldn't stop.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.270
I didn't know any better.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.147
It's really hard, you can't explain it

00:04:28.147 --> 00:04:29.897
unless you go through it, you know.

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:35.090
It's just fucked up my whole life.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:37.600
You know, my family had
family businesses and all that

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.223
and I wasn't a part of it
because I was out using.

00:04:44.266 --> 00:04:46.540
- [Interviewer] What do
you do for money now?

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:51.420
- Whatever I can, I recycle, prostitution,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.483
whatever I can do.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.990
- [Interviewer] That's
dangerous sometimes.

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:58.110
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.940
- [Interviewer] Do you
have any crazy experiences?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:01.773
- A lot.

00:05:01.773 --> 00:05:03.670
A lot, mostly up in the
state of Washington.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.733
I don't know why up there,
but up there was really bad.

00:05:07.644 --> 00:05:09.157
- [Interviewer] Tell me
about what's happened?

00:05:09.157 --> 00:05:11.023
- You know, pull knives, guns.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:15.443
I've just somehow managed
to get away every time.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:19.140
I just knew how to act a certain way

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.080
and distract them, just to pop the door

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.730
and get out of the car, you know?

00:05:25.328 --> 00:05:27.567
- [Interviewer] Well
Cynthia, thank you for that,

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:28.578
I appreciate your time,
good luck out there.

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:29.411
- Okay.

